<!--
  <sui-table> — Ship's reference data-grid primitive.

  Three variants on ONE tag:
  - slot   (default): consumer authors <thead>/<tbody> rows in the light DOM;
            the shadow projects them through named slots.
  - native: consumer authors a full <table> in the light DOM; the shadow only
            frames it (no shadow <table>).
  - data:   engine-backed. The headless `createTable()` engine arrives via
            `prop:table={table}` IDENTITY binding (never a serialized object
            attribute); the windowed body renders `table.centerRows()` through a
            createVirtualizer viewport as a CSS grid. `rows`/`columns` string
            props are an SSR/declarative fallback parsed in the controller.

  Density is the platform axis (`<html data-density>`) — rows read the
  `--density-*` channel directly. There is NO `density`/`dense` prop.

  Events (host.emit): sui-sort {key, direction}, sui-sort-change {sorting},
  sui-row-click {id, index}, sui-row-select {id, selected, selectedIds},
  sui-cell-edit {rowId, columnId, value}.

  NEW SURFACE (re-port from feat/next, parity-gate pass)
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  - No tone prop on this component — rule "tone is global now" doesn't apply.
  - L1 controls were already framework-composed pre-gate (sui-checkbox,
    sui-input, sui-icon, sui-pagination, sui-empty-state) — nothing hand-
    skinned to strip.
  - sx is closed-vocabulary on the two `.empty` divs (slot/native variants);
    the style block keeps the data-variant grid layout, which sx structurally
    cannot express (CSS grid template/auto-columns, position:sticky/absolute,
    pseudo-selectors, @media forced-colors).
  - The variants blocks targeting part=wrap / part=empty (below the props)
    replace the old .sui-table[sticky-header] display:block-on-.wrap and
    .sui-table[data-empty] display-toggle raw selectors.
  - Anatomy (light DOM, class-based — part= left on per the wave sweep note):
    .wrap (root frame) > table/.grid (variant switch) > thead/.grid-head,
    tbody/.viewport > .spacer > .grid-row > .grid-cell; .empty (slot/native
    empty state); .grid-empty (data-variant empty state, wraps sui-empty-state).

  LANG-GAP — no space/dimension token in the ~45–179px range
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  The space scale jumps --control-h-xl (44px) → --panel-min-w-sm (180px); the
  data-grid's feat/next column-min-width (80px, `minmax(80px, 1fr)` on both
  `.grid-head` and `.grid-row`) has no home in the closed vocabulary. Snapped
  to the nearest existing token, --space-8 (40px) — a real ~50% reduction in
  the grid's minimum column floor, not a cosmetic rounding. Reported, not
  routed around with a raw px value. (The 40px gutter/checkbox column DOES
  have an exact match, --space-8 — corrected from the prior pass's wrong pick,
  --control-h-md/34px.)

  LANG-GAP (compiler bug) — `sui-css-token` rejects underscore-suffixed
  fine-step space tokens
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  --space-0_75 (3px) is the EXACT match for the selected-row inset rail (was
  3px in feat/next), but referencing it via var() in a style block fails the
  sui-css-token lint: "unknown CSS token --space-0; did you mean --space-4?".
  Root cause (crates/sui/lint/src/rules/css_token.rs `is_ident_cont`): the
  var()-reference scanner's identifier char-class is
  `[a-z0-9-]`, no `_`, so it truncates the name at the underscore
  (`space-0_75` → `space-0`) — while `crate::tokens::registry()`'s
  *declaration* parser (tokens.rs) DOES accept `_`, so the full name is
  correctly registered and simply never matched against. Every other
  fine-step token (--space-1_25, -1_5, -2_5, -3_5, -4_5) silently survives
  this same bug only because its truncated prefix (space-1/-2/-3/-4) happens
  to ALSO be a valid whole-unit token — --space-0_75 is the one family member
  whose truncated prefix (space-0) isn't (by design: "no --space-0 token
  exists; p:0 must mean zero padding, not a var" — tokens.rs). Kept
  --space-half (2px, the prior pass's pick) rather than the exact match — a
  compiler-level bug, not mine to fix; reported, not routed around.

  LANG-GAP (minor) — no exact 0.06em letter-spacing token
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  --tracking-wide is 0.04em, --tracking-wider is 0.1em; feat/next's column-
  header letter-spacing is 0.06em. Snapped to --tracking-wide (closer of the
  two, off by 0.02em vs 0.04em). Cosmetic; noted for completeness.

  LANG-GAP (compiler bug, HIGHER-severity — found authoring THIS comment) —
  `lower_variants` isn't comment-aware
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  crates/sui/compiler/src/parse/preprocess.rs `lower_variants()` finds the
  next real variants block via a raw source scan for the variants open-tag
  prefix and its matching close-tag, with NO HTML-comment skip — unlike its sibling
  lowering passes in the same file, which all explicitly check
  `source[i..].starts_with("<!--")` and skip the comment body verbatim
  (there's even a regression test guarding the identical failure mode for
  element names, "a CSS comment naming <label> swallowed"). Writing this
  component's own doc comment as prose describing its two variants blocks
  (literally spelling the tag out, e.g. a backtick-quoted
  "variants part=wrap" open-tag) made the scanner treat THAT prose mention
  as the block start, walk forward to the real closing tag of the SECOND
  real block, and splice out everything between — including this comment's
  own closing marker — corrupting the file into an "unterminated comment"
  parse error with no useful diagnostic pointing at the real cause. Worked
  around by rephrasing the doc prose to avoid the literal open-tag spelling;
  the underlying scanner gap is unfixed and will bite the next author who
  documents a variants block by example. Compiler-level, not mine to fix;
  reported, not routed around.
-->

<component>{
  props: {
    variant: 'slot' | 'native' | 'data',
    rows: '',
    columns: '',
    hoverable: true,
    striped: false,
    'sticky-header': false,
    'sticky-first-col': false,
    gutter: false,
    selectable: 'none' | 'single' | 'multi',
    size: 'md' | 'sm' | 'lg',
    label: '',
  },
}</component>
<variants class="wrap">
  sticky-header: overflow-y:auto
</variants>
<variants class="empty">
  data-empty: display:block
</variants>

<style>
  .sui-table {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--density-text);
    color: var(--foreground);
    --table-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    /* Column count drives the data-variant grid track template; set per render
       from colCount(). Declared here so the value resolves without a fallback. */
    --sui-col-count: 1;
  }
  .sui-table[hidden] { display: none; }

  .wrap {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--table-radius);
    background: var(--surface-1);
    /* Frost on glass themes (--card-backdrop-filter is `none` elsewhere).
       isolation establishes a stacking context so the backdrop-filter clips to
       --table-radius — works with the existing overflow:hidden. One change
       covers all rows, which render inside .wrap. */
    backdrop-filter: var(--card-backdrop-filter);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: var(--card-backdrop-filter);
    isolation: isolate;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-xs);
    overflow: hidden;
    overflow-x: auto;
    transition: box-shadow var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }

  table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: separate;
    border-spacing: 0;
    table-layout: auto;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .sui-table[sticky-header] .wrap { max-height: inherit; }

  .empty {
    display: none;
    text-align: center;
  }

  /* ── Data variant — CSS-grid "table" (windowed center band) ─────────────── */
  .grid {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    width: 100%;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .grid-head {
    display: grid;
    grid-auto-flow: column;
    grid-auto-columns: minmax(var(--space-8), 1fr);
    position: sticky;
    top: 0;
    z-index: var(--z-sticky);
    background: var(--surface-2);
    box-shadow: 0 1px 0 0 var(--border);
  }
  .sui-table[gutter] .grid-head,
  .sui-table[gutter] .grid-row {
    grid-template-columns: var(--space-8) repeat(var(--sui-col-count), minmax(var(--space-8), 1fr));
    grid-auto-flow: row;
    grid-auto-columns: auto;
  }
  .col-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-1);
    padding: var(--density-row-py) var(--density-row-px);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wide);
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    white-space: nowrap;
    user-select: none;
  }
  .col-head[data-sort-key] { cursor: pointer; }
  .col-head[data-sort-key]:hover,
  .col-head[aria-sort='ascending'],
  .col-head[aria-sort='descending'] { color: var(--foreground); }
  .col-head sui-icon { color: var(--muted-foreground); }
  .gutter-cell {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 0 var(--space-1);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--divider);
    background: var(--surface-2);
  }
  .filter-row {
    padding: var(--space-1) var(--density-row-px) var(--space-2);
  }
  .viewport {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    overflow-y: auto;
    max-height: var(--panel-max-h-md);
  }
  .spacer {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
  }
  .grid-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-auto-flow: column;
    grid-auto-columns: minmax(var(--space-8), 1fr);
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    width: 100%;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    transition: background-color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }
  .sui-table[hoverable] .grid-row:hover > .grid-cell { background: var(--hover-bg); }
  .grid-row[data-selected] > .grid-cell { background: var(--selected-bg); }
  .grid-row[data-selected] > .grid-cell:first-child { box-shadow: inset var(--space-half) 0 0 0 var(--primary); }
  .grid-row:focus-visible {
    outline: none;
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 var(--ring-width) var(--ring-color);
  }
  .grid-cell {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: var(--density-row-py) var(--density-row-px);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--divider);
    color: var(--foreground);
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .grid-cell.align-right { justify-content: flex-end; }
  .grid-cell.align-center { justify-content: center; }
  .grid-empty {
    padding: var(--space-7) var(--space-5);
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
  }
  .grid-foot {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: var(--space-2) var(--density-row-px);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--surface-2);
  }
  .grid-foot sui-pagination { width: 100%; }

  @media (forced-colors: active) {
    .wrap { border-color: CanvasText; }
    .grid-cell, .col-head { border-bottom-color: CanvasText; }
  }
</style>


<controller>
import { controller, signal, derived, ref, bindNativeEvent } from '@ship/sui-runtime'
import { createTable, type Table } from './engine/create-table'
import { parseJsonColumns, parseJsonRows } from './engine/decode'
import {
  buildViewportVirtualizer,
  headerViews,
  windowRows,
  type AnyRow,
  type HeaderView,
} from './view/wiring'
import { wireDataVariant } from './view/data-events'
import { SUI_TABLE_LIGHT_DOM_CSS, installLightDomStyles } from './view/light-dom-css'

type SortDirection = 'ascending' | 'descending' | 'none'

const ROW_HEIGHT = 40

/** A no-op empty engine so the data-variant scope always has a Table shape to
 *  read (the real engine arrives via the host `table` property or the SSR
 *  `rows`/`columns` fallback). */
function emptyTable(): Table<AnyRow> {
  return createTable<AnyRow>({ data: [], columns: [], getRowId: (r) => r.id })
}

export default controller({
  scope: () => {
    // The live engine. Null until the consumer assigns `prop:table` (the host
    // property, wired in mount) OR the SSR `rows`/`columns` fallback seeds one.
    const tableSig = signal<Table<AnyRow> | null>(null)
    const viewportEl = ref<HTMLDivElement>(null)

    // A stable empty engine backs every read so the template never branches on
    // null; the active engine is `tableSig() ?? EMPTY`.
    const EMPTY = emptyTable()
    const table = derived<Table<AnyRow>>(() => tableSig() ?? EMPTY)

    // The virtualizer windows the center band. `getScrollElement` is the ref
    // thunk (null until bind:this mounts); `count` tracks centerRows().length.
    const virt = buildViewportVirtualizer<AnyRow>(
      () => tableSig(),
      () => viewportEl(),
      ROW_HEIGHT,
    )

    const headers = derived<HeaderView[]>(() => headerViews(table()))
    const windowItems = windowRows<AnyRow>(table, virt.virtualItems)

    const isEmptyInitial = derived<boolean>(() => table().isEmptyInitial())
    const isEmptyFiltered = derived<boolean>(() => table().isEmptyFiltered())
    const rowCount = derived<number>(() => table().rowCount())
    const colCount = derived<number>(() => table().visibleLeafColumns().length)
    const totalSize = virt.totalSize

    // ── Pagination footer (Slice 6) ─────────────────────────────────────────
    // Pagination is opt-in: pageSize 0 = no footer (the full set flows to the
    // virtualizer). When a pageSize is set, the footer <sui-pagination> reads
    // these 1-based views and drives setPageIndex/setPageSize on sui-page-change.
    const hasPagination = derived<boolean>(() => table().state.pagination().pageSize > 0)
    const pageSize = derived<number>(() => table().state.pagination().pageSize)
    const pageIndex1 = derived<number>(() => table().state.pagination().pageIndex + 1)

    return {
      tableSig,
      viewportEl,
      table,
      virt,
      headers,
      windowItems,
      isEmptyInitial,
      isEmptyFiltered,
      rowCount,
      colCount,
      totalSize,
      hasPagination,
      pageSize,
      pageIndex1,
    }
  },

  mount(state, host) {
    // ── prop:table identity wiring ──────────────────────────────────────────
    // The engine is a LIVE JS reference assigned to the host `table` property
    // (never a stringified attribute). Define a property that routes into the
    // scope signal so the windowed render reacts. The `rows`/`columns` string
    // props remain an SSR/declarative fallback (the sui-combobox pattern).
    const adoptTable = (t: Table<AnyRow> | null): void => {
      state.tableSig = t
    }
    Object.defineProperty(host, 'table', {
      configurable: true,
      get: () => state.tableSig,
      set: (t: Table<AnyRow> | null) => adoptTable(t),
    })

    // The reflected `variant` lives on the host attribute (props are not in the
    // typed scope; read the canonical reflected attribute).
    const isData = (): boolean => host.getAttribute('variant') === 'data'

    // SSR fallback: seed an engine from the `rows`/`columns` string props when
    // no identity engine was assigned and the markup carried serialized data.
    if (state.tableSig == null && isData()) {
      const rawRows = parseJsonRows((host as { rows?: string }).rows ?? '')
      const cols = parseJsonColumns((host as { columns?: string }).columns ?? '')
      if (cols.length > 0) {
        adoptTable(
          createTable<AnyRow>({
            data: rawRows,
            columns: cols,
            getRowId: (r) => r.id,
            enableRowSelection: true,
          }),
        )
      }
    }

    installLightDomStyles(host.ownerDocument)

    // ── Data variant: the ONE delegated enhance/emit pipeline + engine reflect ─
    // Installed once; no-ops harmlessly for slot/native (no shadow grid markup).
    const stopDataWiring = wireDataVariant(
      host,
      () => state.tableSig,
      () => state.$signals.windowItems(),
    )

    // ── Slot / native variant enhancement (KEEP — do not disturb) ────────────
    const enhanceSortableHeaders = (): void => {
      host.querySelectorAll<HTMLTableCellElement>('th[data-sort-key]').forEach((th) => {
        if (!th.hasAttribute('aria-sort')) th.setAttribute('aria-sort', 'none')
        if (!th.hasAttribute('tabindex')) th.setAttribute('tabindex', '0')
        if (!th.hasAttribute('role')) th.setAttribute('role', 'columnheader')
      })
    }
    // A "body row" is any data <tr> under the host's table/tbody that is NOT a
    // header row (carries a direct <th>) and NOT the slotted head row. The header
    // exclusion is done in JS — jsdom (the component test env) throws on the
    // `:not(:has(th))` selector, which silently aborted this whole reflect and
    // left [data-empty] unset when only an empty slot was present.
    const findBodyRow = (): Element | null => {
      const candidates = host.querySelectorAll(
        ':scope > table tbody > tr, :scope > table > tr, :scope > tbody > tr, :scope > tr',
      )
      for (const tr of candidates) {
        if (tr.getAttribute('slot') === 'head') continue
        if (tr.querySelector(':scope > th') != null) continue
        return tr
      }
      return null
    }
    const syncEmptyState = (): void => {
      const bodyRow = findBodyRow()
      const hasEmptySlot = host.querySelector('[slot="empty"]') != null
      if (!bodyRow && hasEmptySlot) host.setAttribute('data-empty', '')
      else if (!isData()) host.removeAttribute('data-empty')
    }

    const cycleSlotSort = (th: HTMLTableCellElement): void => {
      const key = th.getAttribute('data-sort-key') || ''
      const current = (th.getAttribute('aria-sort') || 'none') as SortDirection
      const next: SortDirection =
        current === 'none' ? 'ascending' : current === 'ascending' ? 'descending' : 'none'
      host
        .querySelectorAll<HTMLTableCellElement>('th[data-sort-key]')
        .forEach((peer) => peer !== th && peer.setAttribute('aria-sort', 'none'))
      th.setAttribute('aria-sort', next)
      host.emit!('sui-sort', { key, direction: next })
    }

    // Light-DOM (slot/native) header click → sui-sort cycle on the host's own
    // <th>; native row click → sui-row-click. The data variant lives in the
    // shadow root and is handled by the delegated shadow listeners below.
    const onLightClick = (e: MouseEvent): void => {
      const target = e.target as HTMLElement
      const th = target.closest('th[data-sort-key]') as HTMLTableCellElement | null
      if (th && host.contains(th)) {
        cycleSlotSort(th)
        return
      }
      const td = target.closest('td') as HTMLTableCellElement | null
      if (!td || !host.contains(td)) return
      if (td.classList.contains('sui-table-gutter-cell')) return
      const tr = td.closest('tr') as HTMLTableRowElement | null
      const rowId = tr?.getAttribute('data-row-id')
      if (!rowId) return
      host.emit!('sui-row-click', { id: rowId, index: tr!.rowIndex })
    }
    const onLightKey = (e: KeyboardEvent): void => {
      if (e.key !== 'Enter' && e.key !== ' ') return
      const th = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('th[data-sort-key]') as HTMLTableCellElement | null
      if (!th || !host.contains(th)) return
      e.preventDefault()
      cycleSlotSort(th)
    }
    bindNativeEvent(host, 'click', onLightClick as EventListener)
    bindNativeEvent(host, 'keydown', onLightKey as EventListener)

    enhanceSortableHeaders()
    syncEmptyState()
    const observer = new MutationObserver(() => {
      enhanceSortableHeaders()
      syncEmptyState()
    })
    observer.observe(host, { childList: true, subtree: true })

    return () => {
      observer.disconnect()
      stopDataWiring()
      state.virt.dispose()
    }
  },
})

export { SUI_TABLE_LIGHT_DOM_CSS }

</controller>
{#if variant() === 'data'}
<div class="wrap">
  {#if isEmptyInitial()}
    <div class="grid-empty empty" role="status">
      <empty-state data-empty-initial></empty-state>
    </div>
  {:else if isEmptyFiltered()}
    <div class="grid-empty empty" role="status">
      <empty-state>
        <button slot="action" type="button" data-action="clear-filters">Clear filters</button>
      </empty-state>
    </div>
  {:else}
    <div class="grid table" role="grid" aria-label={label() || null} aria-rowcount={rowCount()} aria-colcount={colCount()} aria-multiselectable={selectable() === 'multi' ? 'true' : null}>
      <thead class="grid-head thead" role="row" style:--sui-col-count={colCount()}>
        {#if gutter()}
          <div class="gutter-cell" role="columnheader">
            <input type="checkbox" data-select-all size="sm" aria-label="Select all rows" />
          </div>
        {/if}
        {#for h of headers() key={h.id}}
          <div
            class="col-head"
            role="columnheader"
            data-sort-key={h.sortKey}
            aria-sort={h.canSort ? h.ariaSort : null}
            tabindex={h.canSort ? '0' : null}
          >
            <span>{h.label}</span>
            {#if h.canSort}
              <sui-icon name={h.caret} size="xs" aria-hidden="true"></sui-icon>
            {/if}
            {#if h.canFilter}
              <span class="filter-row" data-filter-col={h.id}>
                <sui-input
                  type="search"
                  size="sm"
                  variant="ghost"
                  placeholder="Filter…"
                  prop:value={h.filterValue}
                ></sui-input>
              </span>
            {/if}
          </div>
        {/for}
      </thead>

      <div class="viewport tbody" role="rowgroup" bind:this={viewportEl}>
        <div class="spacer" style:height={`${totalSize()}px`}>
          {#for w of windowItems() key={w.key}}
            <div
              class="grid-row"
              role="row"
              data-row-id={w.row.id}
              aria-rowindex={w.index + 1}
              tabindex="-1"
              style:transform={`translateY(${w.start}px)`}
              style:--sui-col-count={colCount()}
            >
              {#if gutter()}
                <div class="gutter-cell" role="gridcell">
                  <input
                    type="checkbox"
                    size="sm"
                    data-row-select={w.row.id}
                    prop:disabled={!w.row.selectable}
                    aria-label={`Select row ${w.row.id}`}
                  />
                </div>
              {/if}
              {#for c of w.row.cells key={c.columnId}}
                <div class="grid-cell" role="gridcell" class:align-right={c.align === 'right'} class:align-center={c.align === 'center'}>
                  {c.value}
                </div>
              {/for}
            </div>
          {/for}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    {#if hasPagination()}
      <div class="grid-foot foot">
        <sui-pagination class="pagination" prop:page={pageIndex1()} prop:total={rowCount()} prop:page-size={pageSize()}></sui-pagination>
      </div>
    {/if}
  {/if}
</div>
{:else if variant() !== 'native'}
<div class="wrap">
  <table class="table" aria-label={label() || null}>
    <thead class="thead"><slot name="head"></slot></thead>
    <tbody class="tbody"><slot></slot></tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="empty" role="status" sx="p:7 px:5 text:sm bg:surface-1 fg:muted-foreground">
    <slot name="empty"></slot>
  </div>
</div>
{:else}
<div class="wrap">
  <slot></slot>
  <div class="empty" role="status" sx="p:7 px:5 text:sm bg:surface-1 fg:muted-foreground">
    <slot name="empty"></slot>
  </div>
</div>
{/if}
